.TH LOCK 2
.SH NAME
lock \- lock a process in primary memory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lock(flag)
.SH DESCRIPTION
If the
.I flag
argument is non-zero, the process executing this call will not
be swapped out of memory except if it is required to grow.
If the argument
is zero, the process is
.RB un lock ed.
This call may only be executed by
the super-user or if the caller's group ID is zero.
.PP
Processes are removed from memory when they exit.
.SH BUGS
.BR lock ed
processes interfere with the compaction of primary memory and
can cause deadlock.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Zero is returned if the call is successful; \-1 if not.
.SH ASSEMBLER
(lock = 53.)
.TP
PDP-11:
.nf
sys lock; flag
.fi
.TP
8086:
.nf
BX = 53
AX = flag
int 0Xf1
.fi
.sp
